  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1232 PM MDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nMain vort max will lift to the north during the evening hours \non Monday, with any lingering shower or thunderstorm development\nexpected to push out of the CWA. However, decent moisture will \nremain for much of the night under persistent southwesterly flow\naloft, which could support additional shower development. Given\nthis setup, did keep low chance pops over much of the area.\n\nA drying and warming trend returns for Tuesday through Thursday\nwith mainly isolated thunderstorms possible during the \nafternoons and evenings. Temperatures rebound back into the mid \nto upper 90s by late week. \n\nAnother batch of monsoon moisture spreads northward across CO \nlate week into next weekend in southwesterly flow aloft. This \nshould bring another increase in thunderstorm probabilities \nacross the mountains beginning Friday. Low level moisture \nremains rather lack luster across the plains which should keep \nthunderstorms more isolated and higher based with gusty winds, \nand localized light to moderate rainfall possible. Temperatures \nwill remain above normal.",
